<title>JAPAN: Nippon Mining lowers copper price 10,000 yen/tonne.</title>
<headline>Nippon Mining lowers copper price 10,000 yen/tonne.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Mining and Metals Co said on Monday it lowered its selling price for electrolytic copper by 10,000 yen to 300,000 yen per tonne, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Major Japanese smelters periodically review their selling prices, changing them in line with market prices and currency rates.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
